            <ArticleTitle>Unusual cause of pleuritic chest pain in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2016217307</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2016-217307</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 5-year-old boy with hereditary multiple exostoses who presented with left-sided pleuritic chest pain. A CT scan of the chest revealed an intrathoracic exostosis in close association with the heart.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2016 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
